### FacultySync REST API tests
### Open this file in IntelliJ and click the green ▶ next to each request.
### Start both services first (run configuration "FacultySync (All Services)").

@faculty = http://localhost:8081/api
@ai = http://localhost:8082/api

### ===================== Faculty Management Service (8081) =====================

### 1. List all faculty
GET {{faculty}}/faculty

### 2. Get one faculty member
GET {{faculty}}/faculty/2

### 3. Add a new faculty member
POST {{faculty}}/faculty
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Prof. Ravi Teja",
  "department": "CSE",
  "email": "ravi@college.edu",
  "designation": "Assistant Professor",
  "subjects": ["DBMS", "Data Structures"]
}

### 3a. Edit a faculty member
PUT {{faculty}}/faculty/8
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Prof. Fatima Khan",
  "department": "CSE",
  "email": "fatima@college.edu",
  "designation": "Associate Professor",
  "subjects": ["Algorithms", "Java Programming", "Data Structures", "DBMS"]
}

### 3b. Delete a faculty member (blocked with 409 if they still have periods, leaves or substitutions)
DELETE {{faculty}}/faculty/9

### 4. Weekly workload of every faculty (facultyId -> classes)
GET {{faculty}}/faculty/workload

### 5. Full timetable
GET {{faculty}}/timetable

### 6. Timetable of one faculty
GET {{faculty}}/timetable?facultyId=2

### 6a. Add a timetable period (409 if the faculty or the class is already busy at that time)
POST {{faculty}}/timetable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "facultyId": 4,
  "day": "FRIDAY",
  "period": 5,
  "subject": "DBMS",
  "className": "CSE-3A",
  "room": "103"
}

### 6b. Edit a timetable period (e.g. move it to period 6)
PUT {{faculty}}/timetable/24
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "facultyId": 4,
  "day": "FRIDAY",
  "period": 6,
  "subject": "DBMS",
  "className": "CSE-3A",
  "room": "103"
}

### 6c. Delete a timetable period
DELETE {{faculty}}/timetable/24

### 7. Apply for leave (status = PENDING)
POST {{faculty}}/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "facultyId": 5,
  "fromDate": "2026-11-05",
  "toDate": "2026-11-06",
  "reason": "Medical leave"
}

### 8. All leave requests (optionally ?status=PENDING / APPROVED / REJECTED)
GET {{faculty}}/leaves

### 9. HOD approves leave #1
PUT {{faculty}}/leaves/1/approve

### 10. HOD rejects leave #2
PUT {{faculty}}/leaves/2/reject

### 11. Classes affected by leave #1
GET {{faculty}}/leaves/1/affected-classes

### 12. Faculty free on a date & period (change the date to an upcoming Monday)
GET {{faculty}}/faculty/available?date=2026-11-02&period=2

### ======================== AI Substitute Service (8082) ========================

### 13. AI recommendations for every class affected by leave #1
###     (this service internally calls the Faculty Service over REST)
GET {{ai}}/recommendations/leave/1

### 14. Explain the scoring model
GET {{ai}}/recommendations/model

### ======================= Final decision by the HOD =======================

### 15. Confirm a substitute (copy slotId/date from request 13)
POST {{faculty}}/substitutes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaveId": 1,
  "slotId": 3,
  "date": "2026-11-02",
  "substituteFacultyId": 8
}

### 16. All confirmed substitutions
GET {{faculty}}/substitutes
